uation we play  as an Interstellar Freight transporter  in the year 2320 and then of course  things go wrong and we must survive an  alien invasion which mutates the  inhabitants of a prison we must go  through using anything we can get our  hands on to survive such as the grip gun  a gravity gun that lets us pick up  objects and enemies and use them as a  shield or just yank them across the room  with their limbs flying off lovely of  course that's only one way to approach  encounters we've also seen devastating  melee attacks subtle Stealth gameplay  and we are told it's all linked to skill  trees for progression the Callisto  protocol is heavily emphasizing the  importance of story and to back that up  a few big name actors from film and TV  are on board with the project the battle  with dead space Starts Now the Callisto  protocol releases on December 2nd on the  PlayStations the Xboxes and the PC  December will also see The Return of the  Need for Speed series Unbound changes  the tone and feel of the franchise and  it kinda looks anime at its core it's  more Need for Speed you've played for  years racing by day and night in which  cops are itching to take you down  Unbound has confirmed over 140 cars  including many licenses from Aston  Martin Ford McLaren and Porsche to name  a few customization is a huge part of  the game with access to tuning and body  kits for all vehicles creating thousands  of potential setups and combinations for  those people who really want to be fully  in control of their ride the story kicks  off with two friends running an auto  shop and after a burglary they must take  part in illegal races to win back their  stolen gear and of course they get  hooked on that adrenaline and keep going  multiplayer modes have been confirmed in  the open world city and hey if you're  getting flashbacks to the cop AI in  older games you should know that police  AI is now adjustable the Kamikaze cops  are definitely an issue of the past Need  for Speed Unbound is the third game in a  row dropping on December 2nd but this  time only the PS5 Xbox series and PC are  confirmed last gen consoles Abby left  behind  back in 2007 a portable Final Fantasy  game called Crisis Core released on the  PSP a much-loved game on a relatively  small platform which branched out the  Final Fantasy VII story now in 2022 the  game has been remastered adapted and  evolved into Crisis Core Final Fantasy  VII reunion that's a lot of words acting  as a prequel to Final Fantasy VII in  fact seven years prior to that story  revolving all around Zack a pivotal  character in The overarching Narrative  who has a past shrouded in mystery and  now it's time to see it from his point  of view for fans of Final Fantasy 7  remake reunion is a must play game  reunion releases on December 13th on  Playstation Xbox PC and twitch at 50 50  pounds or 60 Euros so a little less than  a full price game  [Music]  A reduced price game you may want to  know about is hello neighbor 2. the  original game was a clever take on  breaking into a neighbor's home to find  out their Eerie Secrets the idea was  good the implementation was not so good  well finally after many iterations and  improvements it's time for hello  neighbor too this time we play as a  journalist who comes to town in the  pursuit of a story The call gameplay is  then stealth horror we must break into  houses around the neighborhood as their  owners pursuers here's the best bit  those people will adapt to your actions  for instance if you constantly come in  at night time they'll sleep during the  day so they'll be alert the moment you  venture onto their property when chased  they'll look in more realistic places  and if you hide in the same place more  than once it's likely they will figure  that out as you adapt they adapt keeping  the gameplay Dynamic and that feeling of  uncertainty and anxiety constantly with  you if you want to break and Enter look  out for hello neighbor 2 on December 6th  on Playstation Xbox and PC  [Music]  okay let's do some free stuff and it's a  really weird month for free games first  a few games that released after last  month video Destroy All Humans clone  Carnage is totally free on Steam it's  totally free on Xbox but for some reason  on Playstation it costs 2 cents in the  US 25 cent in Europe and here in the UK  it costs 20 pence I have no idea why a  standalone multiplayer mode supporting  four players online or two in local  co-op split screen with six maps and  four game modes to play it's basically  some dumb Alien Invasion fun with  friends for a few evenings it won't last  you forever but it's a good change of  pace and it also has the platinum trophy  that's your jam next Gundam Evolution  official releases on November the 30th  or December the 1st depending on where  you live in the world it's a six on six  Arena shooter focusing solely on Gundam  mobile suits and their fighting prowess  the devs have worked on a Boost system  to accelerate your Gundam towards fight  or to evade attacks and that leads into  a class system where different Gundams  have slightly different properties it's  quite usual if your suit has more Health  you are expected to play as a tank and  protect your teammates and gain aggro  the supports have healing abilities and  everyone else is there to fire as many  bullets as possible to achieve the  objective with overwatch's recent  Revival and going free to play Gundam  Evolution will need all the players it  can so if this is appealing to you you  hold the power to keep it alive on  Playstation Xbox and PC  oh I did intend to tell you about a  Japanese MMORPG which made its way over  to console last month internal Kingdom  battle Peak it's known as a PC and  mobile game which is trying to add more  platforms from for its player base with  cross play and cross progression Eternal  Kingdom follows the usual High fantasy  MMO tropes by creating a character with  a certain playstyle and taking on  missions in this vastly open world I'd  love to tell you about how great the  gameplay is but here in the UK the game  was removed from the PlayStation Store  I've reached out to find out why yet  nothing has returned to me it's been  suggested December will see it returned  from what I'm told though the na version  is up and running quite smoothly so it's  an option if you're looking for a new  MMO on mobile PC and console right now  [Music]  oh did you hear the news about the  Witcher 3 check your game's collection  dust it off because if you own that game  from many years ago you'll be granted a  free upgrade to the next gen version on  PS5 and Xbox series on December 14th The  Witcher 3 world Hunt is one of the  highest rated RPGs ever made and now  it's back the update adds improved  Graphics Lighting and Sound mods and  also new DLC tied to the Netflix TV show  if you don't know we play as geralt a  Witcher who takes on many missions to  slay beasts in the open world whilst the  constant pressure of the hunt chasing  down Siri is upon them Siri is  effectively garop's adopted daughter the  original game took around 50 hours to  finish and it was amazing oh and uh Pro  tip if you don't own the physical game  but don't want to pay full price for the  new version then look around your local  second-hand game store to find it for a  few dollars pounds of euros and then the  questions will begin is The Witcher 3  the greatest RPG of all time so that's  December what you playing I'm definitely  going back to The Witcher what about you  I'm Adam you're awesome I'll see you  next time  [Music]

